# Scratch/disposable trees parked in the shared master worktree. NEVER commit these:
# a 272 MiB full-repo snapshot tarball sat here untracked-and-un-ignored (INT-042), one
# `git add -A` away from permanent history bloat.
_to_delete/

# Lane-lock flock sidecars written by scripts/claim_lane_lock.py. They are
# per-machine runtime state, and a stray one at the repo root has now shown up
# in `git status` across three consecutive session reports (339S, 339T, 340)
# without ever being actionable — noise that trains readers to skim the untracked
# list, which is where a real stray file hides.
*.claimlock

# Generated calibration report. Three scripts write this exact root path
# (calibration_analysis.py, build_calibration_report.py, build_calibration_report_svg.py),
# which is how a 2026-05-26 snapshot got committed and then sat at the repo root for three
# months reading like a current report. Snapshots belong in docs/archive/ under a dated
# name, added deliberately with `git add -f`.
/calibration_report.html

# Evidence HTML written INTO the repo root by the frontend capture tests
# (`frontend/__tests__/capture/*.test.tsx` resolve `../../../artifacts-ux-pNNN`).
# Running `npx jest` — a mandatory gate — therefore dirties whichever worktree
# ran it, and the shared lane trees are where that lands. Four such directories
# sat untracked in `bainluck-dev/latency` long enough that a session's real
# uncommitted work hid in the same `git status` list (LAT-P197). A gate must not
# be able to redden the tree it runs in. Nothing under these paths has ever been
# tracked; deliberate evidence can still be committed with `git add -f`.
/artifacts-ux-*/
.env*

# CAL-P992: a LIVE append-only cursor, not a bankable artifact — a watcher is still
# writing to it every ~3 minutes, so tracking it leaves every worktree permanently
# dirty. The evidence CAL-P989 cites (after-needle.json, first-published-payload.json,
# PUBLISHED.marker, the PNGs) is committed; the moving tail is not.
artifacts/cal-p989/bank-cursor.jsonl

# CAL-P998 / CERT-863 follow-up: `backend/artifacts/` is a CWD ACCIDENT, not a home.
# Nothing under it had ever been tracked until this branch swept 89 cal-996 beat
# captures (80,496 lines) into a two-file sweep fix, and 72 more were sitting
# untracked beside them from the same still-running watcher. Two separate causes,
# one directory:
#
#   1. Evidence captures written next to whatever `cd backend` shell produced them.
#      Evidence belongs in `.claude/handoff/ARTIFACT-*`, which is where cal-996's
#      own cert evidence already lives.
#   2. `scripts/calibration_scorecard.py --record` resolves its history path
#      RELATIVE TO CWD, so running it from `backend/` silently forks a SECOND
#      series here while the canonical `artifacts/calibration-scorecard/history.jsonl`
#      at the repo root goes un-appended — no error, exit 0. That fork had two real
#      datapoints (2026-08-02, 2026-09-02) that the canonical series was missing;
#      they were folded back in and the fork deleted. Run the scorecard from the
#      REPO ROOT.
#
# Ignoring the directory is what stops the next `git add -A` from re-committing it.
# Deliberate evidence can still be committed with `git add -f`.
backend/artifacts/
